      "type": "explain",
      "id": "e1",
      "title": "aller + infinitive: a plan for soon",
      "body": "Use the present of aller plus another verb in its infinitive to say what you are going to do. It is a common way to talk about a planned or near-future action."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "t1",
      "title": "aller + a verb in its infinitive",
      "headers": [
        "Person",
        "aller",
        "Plan"
